  "review_notes": [
    "Reviewed the current top-level proposal.json in full, not merely the prior-result proposal supplied by context. Also read functionality.md, both complete disposition ledgers, coverage.json and unresolved.json.",
    "All three proposed writes concern owned subjects and are supported by canonical source. The PURIN flag consumer uses a strict top-boundary comparison after exclusion and side-boundary checks. ReflectAttr.x1A3C_damageOver selects the forwarding wrapper in Fighter_ProcessHit_8006D1EC. The physics correction correctly distinguishes animation-to-Fall from collision-to-Down.",
    "The active motion table associates ShieldBreakFly with the four owned callbacks. Rendered aliases were not used as independent proof of action identity or helper semantics.",
    "Acceptance preserves the explicit deferral of four section-owned facts, the wrapper-purpose record's unsupported stack-padding rationale, and the IASA shield-break-stun concept link. Acceptance does not promote those claims as established.",
    "Retained upward-launch descriptions denote ordinary configured gameplay, not unconditional positivity or eventual landing. IASA non-interruption is limited to this hook. Collision transition descriptions are limited to the supplied callback and normal completion; the grounding assertion and unknown query side effects remain qualified.",
    "Additional independent inspection of ftCommon_ApplyFrictionAir confirms that it writes a friction contribution to x74_anim_vel.x rather than directly attenuating self_vel.x. At equal absolute friction and velocity it selects -self_vel.x. Negative or exceptional friction can invalidate ordinary attenuation assumptions. The proposal's shared-friction wording remains accurate; detailed integration and exceptional-value guarantees are not promoted.",
    "No replacement proposal, unowned write, entity creation, merge, new link or artifact mutation is included."
  ],
